Per-interface hardening sysctls are applied per attached vif device by
vif-route-qubes.  Native Guix templates have no systemd-sysctl, so route that
call to the qubes-network-interface-sysctl helper installed by this channel,
preserving the per-vif behavior.

Guix-specific: no systemd; per-vif sysctls applied by a Guile helper.
Upstream file: qubes-core-agent-linux network/vif-route-qubes

diff --git a/network/vif-route-qubes b/network/vif-route-qubes
index 580ddd0..ae93235 100755
--- a/network/vif-route-qubes
+++ b/network/vif-route-qubes
@@ -182,7 +182,7 @@ qubesdb_read_bool () {
 # Harden against various attacks if requested
 if [[ "$command" = 'online' ]] &&
     qubesdb_read_bool /qubes-service/harden-network-interfaces 1; then
